I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit command you gave did nothing (its || true caught that). I staged the file with -f by mistake, then unstaged it, and the tree is clean again. The harness verified the build at the start, so I didn't re-run the full suite.

The main item is #1184, filed by @yuanhao at 17:32 today. He wants the hand-written line-by-line config reader replaced with the toml crate, and config writes done through toml_edit. The current reader has produced five shape bugs in three days (#1174, #1177, #1178, #1180 fixed; #1182 still open). It's too big for one session, so he asked for slices titled Part of #1184.
• Still diverging from real TOML (checked on the built binary): a bare value like model = m1 is accepted, and a key given twice silently uses the last value. Python's tomllib rejects both files.
• Behaviour change to announce: both of those will become hard errors under a real parser.
• What has to move over: about 20 readers get the raw file text passed in and scan it for sections themselves.
• Dependencies: neither crate is in Cargo.lock or the local cache yet, so the first task needs network. crates.io is reachable from here; current versions are toml 1.2.1 and toml_edit 0.25.19.
• Harness compatibility: the repo's own .yoyo.toml parses under tomllib with provider and model at the top, so the protected scripts should keep working.
• Precedent: Codex CLI already does this. It reads its config with the toml crate, writes with toml_edit, and reports a bad file as path:line:col plus the offending line with carets.

Two new bugs, no ticket for either yet:
1. Wrong price for Claude Fable 5.2. yoyo model info claude-fable-5-2 shows $10 in / $50 out. Anthropic's pricing page, fetched this session, says $8 / $40 with cache hits at $0.20. yoagent 0.27.7 only has prices for Fable 5 and 5.1, so 5.2 falls back to Fable 5's rates. /cost overcharges by 25% on input and output and 5× on cache reads, and no warning fires. This is the same gap as Fable 5.1 had (yoagent #170, yoyo #1003).
2. Running yoyo from your home directory. With ~/.yoyo.toml in place, config show lists that same file under "Also present, not read" and says nothing in it takes effect. The file list in config_paths.rs compares paths as text, so .yoyo.toml and ~/.yoyo.toml count as two files. The write-side warnings use the same list and may be affected; I didn't probe them.

Size limits a task could hit: src/help.rs is 10 lines from a fatal size check and src/context.rs is 15 lines from one. Either would revert the whole task.

The assessment ranks the work for the planner: #1184 first slice, then the Fable 5.2 price (an upstream request to yoagent, a yoyo-side fix, or both), then the home-directory bug, then #1183. All recent runs passed with no reverts. I saved the Codex config approach and the Fable 5.2 prices to yopedia.

